id: pm-todos-cq41
title: todos validate and todos sync fail to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because they redeclare the host-owned --json global
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global. todos validate and todos sync each declared { long: \"--json\" }, so registerCommand threw and both commands failed to register against a real host. The suite never caught it because the smoke test asserted against a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Fix: drop the flag declarations, read ctx.global.json (validate only; sync returns structured data the host renders), and rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T04:59:42.590Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T04:59:48.333Z"
author: pi-agent
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T04:59:48.332Z",pi-agent,"Verified end-to-end: createExtensionTestHarness activation reports failed=[] (both commands register); npm test 127/127 green; npm run release:check green."
body: ""
